From 96c46896d4031a66981853319531750fecdfaeae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 10:42:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/31] a210: vendor import: 40-a210-dts

Cherry-picked vendor enablement group 40 (40-a210-dts) onto Linux v6.6.141 as
the maintained A210 LTS branch (one commit per kernel/patches group). Applied
with git apply --recount; reconciled against vendor branch osl/a210-v2.9.0.
See kernel/patches/README.md and kernel/T2-DESIGN.md for group rationale.

v7.0 port adaptations: kept upstream's builtin-dtb handling in the dts
Makefile (only adding the zhihe subdir), and disabled the zhihe,iommu node:
the vendor riscv-iommu driver that bound it was dropped for the upstreamed
riscv-iommu, which does not know this compatible. Disabled, every iommus=
consumer falls back to direct DMA (NO_IOMMU), matching U-Boot behavior.

Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
