+/*
+ * OSL: drop pmic-supply on power_gpu / power_npu_wrapper / power_vp_wrapper.
+ *
+ * The a210-pd driver iterates ALL child power-domain nodes during probe and
+ * returns -EPROBE_DEFER as soon as a `pmic-supply` regulator phandle can't be
+ * resolved. dvdd_gpu_reg / dvdd_npu_vip_reg / dvdd_vp_reg are PMIC outputs --
+ * we don't have the PMIC driver path wired up yet, so the regulator framework
+ * never produces them and the a210-pd probe defers forever. That cascades:
+ * the console UART (uart4 at 0x08401000) depends on power_peri2 from this
+ * same provider, so /dev/console can't open, /init's exec redirect fails,
+ * and the kernel panics with exitcode=2.
